  "interview": {
    "expected_score": 24,
    "expected_score_probability": 55,
    "full_score_probability": 1,
    "hardest_part": "Advancing through mid- and late-game research and infrastructure. Each building requires navigating several menu layers one click at a time, and mid-game milestones (electrolyzer, smart batteries, coal generator reaching 50000 J, rock crusher, exosuit forge) depend on research trees and interconnected power, gas, and liquid systems that each need multiple distinct construction and wiring steps before they function.",
    "likely_failure": "Power infrastructure. Getting a manual or coal generator built, wired to a battery, and producing the threshold electricity requires queuing and completing several buildings in the right order, with duplicants correctly prioritized. A mis-click in the wire tool, a priority misconfiguration, or an oxygen/food crisis pulling duplicants off construction will stall progress and consume the available wall-clock budget.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Native pause lets me study the full screenshot before committing each action, so I can plan without time pressure. Duplicants auto-execute any reachable queued job, meaning once a build order is correctly placed and materials exist, no further input is needed until it completes. The Terra start provides abundant sandstone, copper, and iron near the surface, which covers most early-tier buildings. Many of the first ten milestones need only one correctly placed building each.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Single-action-per-turn makes menu navigation expensive: opening Build, choosing a category, selecting a building, and clicking the placement tile each consume a separate turn, so queuing five buildings takes twenty or more turns. The research tree requires a research station to be built and staffed before any technology unlocks, adding a prerequisite chain before mid-game milestones become accessible. Duplicant needs (food, morale, oxygen) run continuously and can trigger crises that force reactive management, diverting turns away from construction. Late-game milestones require refined metals, plastic, and steel whose production chains each span multiple buildings and technologies, making them very hard to reach within a 3-hour wall-clock budget under one-action-per-screenshot constraints."
  }
